{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Desire","html":"<article id='sn1.78'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 1.78 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 1.78 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>8. Chetvāvagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>8. Slain </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kāmasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Desire </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Kimatthakāmo na dade, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“What should one who wants what’s best <j>not give away? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kiṁ macco na pariccaje; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What should a mortal not forsake? </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kiṁsu muñceyya kalyāṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What should be released when it’s good, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pāpikaṁ na ca mocaye”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>but not when it’s bad?” </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Attānaṁ na dade poso, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“A man shouldn’t give away himself. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attānaṁ na pariccaje; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>He shouldn’t forsake himself. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vācaṁ muñceyya kalyāṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Speech should be released when it’s good, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pāpikañca na mocaye”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>but not when it’s bad.” </span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
